# Secrets. Never commit the real .env -- .env.example (checked in) is the
# only one that belongs in git; it holds named placeholders, not values.
.env

# Credentials this repo's own code writes at runtime (src/upstox/session.py
# CREDENTIALS_PATH), in case a native install's config dir ever ends up
# inside a checkout instead of $HOME.
upstox_credentials.json

# Native install. Created by setup.sh; installs pinned
# dependencies from requirements.txt, never something to commit.
.venv/

# Python bytecode / caches -- regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The database this repo's own code creates (SPOT_DB_PATH, or the default
# quickstart path used in README examples) -- real market data, and the
# whole point of this repo is that it never ships any. WAL/SHM are SQLite's
# own auxiliary files alongside the main database file (see
# src/db/connection.py's WAL-mode connection factory) and must be ignored
# together with it -- a .db without its live .db-wal is not a consistent
# snapshot.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Rendered chart output (src/render/chart.py::render_candles, the `chart`
# CLI command's --out). Generated from whatever's in the local database;
# never something to check in. If this repo ever legitimately ships a real
# image (a docs illustration, say), add it with `git add -f`.
*.svg
*.png

# Internal QA/handoff notes -- useful locally, not for publication.
HANDOFF.md
